nd empowering a community where learning flourishes. We believe that the talented, motivated and creative employees at Keystone College are our greatest asset. Student Employment Learn more about work study and student employment. Employee benefits package. We offer a comprehensive employee benefits package and much more. Health insurance Dental insurance Vision insurance Group life insurance AFLAC Insurance Retirement plan Paid time off benefits including: Sick leave Vacation Funeral leave Jury duty tuition Additional employee benefits On site child care Free parking Wellness center Library Credit unions Employee discounts Keystone College tuition remission Tuition exchange How to apply for a job at Keystone. To apply for a position at Keystone College, email or mail a cover letter, resume and 3 professional references to: Human Resources Keystone College PO Box 50 One College Green La Plume, PA 18440 Email Human Resources Work Study or Part-time Student Employment Positions Learn how to apply for Work Study and Part-time Student Employment positions. All Jobs Head Men’s Volleyball Coach / Sports Information Assistant July 29, 2026 Field Supervisors & Student Teaching Supervisors July 7, 2026 Adjunct Faculty – Law May 18, 2026 Graduate Assistant: Student Life May 14, 2026 Innovative Technology Integrator/Software Implementation Specialist March 19, 2026 Teacher II May 22, 2025 Teacher I May 22, 2025 Assistant Professor of Counseling (Tenure-Track) April 10, 2025 No jobs at this time. Annual Security & Fire Safety Report (ASFSR) The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report includes statistics concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by Keystone College, and on property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus. This report also includes campus safety policies such as campus access, sexual assault, reporting crimes, and more. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report 2025-2026 (PDF) Annual Security and Fire Safety Report 2024-2025 (PDF) Annual Security and Fire Safety Report 2023-2024 (PDF) Annual Security and Fire Safety Report 2022-2023 (PDF) Annual Security and Fire Safety Report 2021-2022 (PDF) Annual Security and Fire Safety Report 2020-2021 (PDF) Annual Security and Fire Safety Report 2019-2020 (PDF) Annual Security and Fire Safety Report 2018-2019 (PDF) Annual Security and Fire Safety Report 2017-2018 (PDF) Annual Security and Fire Safety Report 2016-2017 (PDF) Annual Security and Fire Safety Report 2015-2016 (PDF) Annual Security and Fire Safety Report 2014-2015 (PDF) Annual Security and Fire Safety Report 2023-2014 (PDF) The Keystone College Department of Campus Safety prepares this report to comply with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics. Stop Campus Hazing Act Click here for reports of hazing. Founded in 1868 and accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education. Maps and Directions. Office Hours: Monday-Friday 8:30 a.m. – 4:30 p.m. One College Green P.O. Box 50 La Plume, PA 18440-0200 1-800-824-2764 or 570-945-8000 Apply Visit Campus Need help? Bookstore Buy Keystone Gear Careers at Keystone College Current Students & Staff Departments and Office Hours Library Student Consumer Information Web Content Policy Web Accessibility Statement Web Disclaimer and Privacy Statement"
